plishment of longevity isn't unparalleled, her nearly perfect bill of health has amazed doctors.  I met with Jones to find out what it takes to be a supercentenarian."}, {"time": "41000", "image": "engenn8le12ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Throughout her life, Jones has lived simply: no parties, smoking, alcohol or drugs. Jones' daily regimen is uncomplicated. Every morning with a glass of water, she is supposed to take her blood-pressure medication and a multivitamin. She is supposed to see the doctor every 3 months for \"maintenance\", she said.  Jones' diet consists largely of fruit. To the bewilderment of her physicians, Jones has even appeared to be \"reverse aging.\" Over the last four years, her hair has changed from gray to brown and softened."}, {"time": "76250", "image": "engenn8le12ob03re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "The question is: How are we supposed to live to achieve a life likes Jones'? Does diet and lifestyle contribute to longevity, or is it a genetic lottery? <br/>\nThe research is inconclusive, but it suggests that supercentenarians have a complicated genetic makeup that helps them avoid age-related diseases."}]}}]}]}], "type": "sena"}